Well, I just ascended a Samurai, after the Valkyrie and Barbarian.  
It's about time, too, since I've lost 3 high level characters.  The 
high-level graveyard:

1) Caveman, choked to death on a tin of troll meat, AC -22, D. Level 52
2) Wizard, petrified by a cockatrice corpse (from falling), w/ book of the dead
3) Healer, starved to death (Famine), w/ Amulet, Astral Plane

This game, on the other hand, was a cakewalk.  Got a wish from a demon on 
the oracle level, and +2 grey dragon scale mail.  Also got poison resistance
from a cave spider early on, so I was playing with all the advantages
of the barbarian.  Sac'ed for Snickersnee, threw away Ogresmasher, 
whipped through the mines, and sat on a throne which granted me my wish of
Grayswandir.  Dipped for Excalibur, sac'ed again for Sunsword(which joined
Ogresmasher and Snickersnee), and stormed the Castle.  Found FOUR magic
lamps in the game, used one for light and the other three for a blessed
scroll of charging, blessed amulet of magical breathing, and blessed ring
of levitation.  Went back up and completed the Quest, snagging the Tsurugi...
and one comment.  THAT WEAPON KICKS BUTT.  Almost made me wish I had wished
for it with my other lawful characters.  Descended Gehennom using spellbooks
of magic mapping (aided by two magic markers I found in the tool shop).  
Killed Vlad with 3 swipes and sat on Vlad's throne, and guess what, 
another wish!  This went for another blessed magic marker(can never have too
many, and better than a genocide scroll wish).  Down on level 55 with no
descending staircase, I zapped detect treasure and started looking for the
vibrating square.  Imagine my surprise when I move on a wand and get 

"You see a wand of wishing."

After wishing for more scrolls of charging and charging it up, I waltzed thru
the Sanctum and fled with my trusty helm of opposite alignment (found very
early on) and my newly wished for ring of teleport control(I was carrying
around 6 wands of teleportation and 20 scrolls).  Orcus's wand of death with 
7 charges stood me in good stead for the Wizard...except the time he 
summoned a cockatrice which I used to stone him with.  Grabbed the crystal 
ball I had left on Medusa's isle, and used it on the Elemental planes for 
a quick exit.  I finally made it to the Astral Plane and sure enough, my 
god's temple was the last one I visited.

Final score : 3.6 million in 62000-odd moves, and 8 excess wishes.  Also
found Cleaver and Orcrist on the Astral Plane, bringing the artifact weapon
count to 7.  No cursed bell, no poly-piling(no wand of polymorph), no
wishing for quest artifacts, no backups.

Boy, I'm sure going to miss that Tsurugi.
